    {
      "line": 95,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 2: ZERATHUNE - CRYSTAL OF EARTH"
    },
    {
      "line": 97,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Zerathune was not fighting."
    },
    {
      "line": 98,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was persuading."
    },
    {
      "line": 100,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They found him in a shattered basin, his verdant scales the only green in a landscape of black glass and red flame."
    },
    {
      "line": 101,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He had his claws sunk deep into the bedrock, his body vibrating with a low, sub-sonic frequency."
    },
    {
      "line": 102,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Before him, a massive tectonic fault line was slowly, agonizingly, knitting itself back together."
    },
    {
      "line": 104,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He did not stop his work as they landed. “Aelxion’s scent is on you."
    },
    {
      "line": 105,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "You seek the Terros Crystal.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 107,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“We do,” Geralt said."
    },
    {
      "line": 109,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“You understand what it is?” Zerathune’s voice was the grind of continental plates—patient, immense, and tired. “It is not a rock."
    },
    {
      "line": 110,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It is a binding agreement."
    },
    {
      "line": 111,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "My geomantic resonance given solid form."
    },
    {
      "line": 112,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It tells stone how to be stone."
    },
    {
      "line": 113,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It tells fractures they are whole."
    },
    {
      "line": 114,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "I have worn it for eight centuries.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 116,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He finally lifted his head, emerald eyes regarding them. “Giving it to you does not merely disarm me."
    },
    {
      "line": 117,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It scars me."
    },
    {
      "line": 118,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Severs a part of my soul from the earth-song."
    },
    {
      "line": 119,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It will shorten my lifespan by centuries."
    },
    {
      "line": 120,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The stone will forget my name sooner.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 122,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Oreck stepped forward, his scales dusty with ash. “How much time do you lose?”"
    },
    {
      "line": 124,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“Three hundred years."
    },
    {
      "line": 125,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Perhaps four.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 127,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“And if the planet’s core regulation fails?"
    },
    {
      "line": 128,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "How much time does everything lose?”"
    },
    {
      "line": 130,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Zerathune was silent."
    },
    {
      "line": 131,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The ground beneath them trembled, not from instability, but from his consideration."
    },
    {
      "line": 133,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He is the earth’s memory, Green rumbled, a profound respect in the bond."
    },
    {
      "line": 134,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "To ask this of him is to ask a mountain to forget its own peak."
    },
    {
      "line": 136,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“A shorter life on a living world,” Zerathune said at last, the words heavy as bedrock, “beats an immortality of echoes on dead ash.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 138,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "With a sound of deep, personal rupture, a scale over his heart split open."
    },
    {
      "line": 139,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "From it, he drew the Terros Crystal."
    },
    {
      "line": 141,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was dense, brown, and seemingly inert—until you held it."
    },
    {
      "line": 142,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then you felt the thrum, the deep, structural pulse of a planet’s heartbeat."
    },
    {
      "line": 143,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was stability incarnate."
    },
    {
      "line": 145,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "As the crystal left his grasp, Zerathune visibly dimmed."
    },
    {
      "line": 146,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The vibrant green of his scales dulled towards olive."
    },
    {
      "line": 147,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The fault line before him groaned, but held."
    },
    {
      "line": 148,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He had given them his foundation."
    },
    {
      "line": 150,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“Do not let my sacrifice be for cinders,” he whispered, before turning back to his work, his song to the earth now fainter, more fragile."
    }
  ],
